Limitations
  - LOGO holds out one chemical system while its elements stay in training (N-Ti out,
    Ti and C-Ti in): it tests an unseen SYSTEM, not an unseen ELEMENT. The element
    split above is the harder test.
  - For elemental systems E_hull == E_form exactly, so the E_hull <= 1.0 eV/atom filter
    truncates their target range; R2 is scale-dependent, so these R2 values are not
    comparable with an unfiltered study.

